# Every `resource_type` written into `audit_log`, classified by whether it denotes a NATURAL PERSON.
#
# Why this file exists: GDPR erasure of the resource axis is the owning bounded context's job
# (docs/adr/audit-activity-log.md D4). That assignment only works if "is this type a person?" is a
# declared, reviewed decision — otherwise a new person-denoting type ships with nobody erasing it, and
# the subject's real id survives their own erasure beside their pseudonym.
#
# Format, one per line:
#   <ResourceType> => non-person
#   <ResourceType> => person :: <path of the erasure use case that anonymises it>
#
# The gate (PersonResourceErasureGateTest, run by `make php.lint.audit-resource`) fails the build when a
# type reaches `AuditResource::of(...)` or a route's `_audit_resource_type` default without a line here,
# and when a `person` line names a file that does not wire AuditResourceAnonymiser. It cannot judge the
# classification itself — that is what review is for.

Bank => non-person
BankAccount => non-person
User => person :: src/Iam/Identity/Application/FulfilIdentityErasure.php
